================================================================================
Bundled WCAG 2.2 dataset (the worldwide core)
================================================================================

The file src/data/wcag.json is derived from the official Web Content Accessibility
Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 source published by the World Wide Web Consortium (W3C).

Source: https://github.com/w3c/wcag  (guidelines/ success-criterion fragments)
Spec:   https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/

WCAG 2.2 is © W3C and is reused here under the W3C Document License
(https://www.w3.org/copyright/document-license/). ultra11y reproduces the
success-criterion ids, titles and conformance levels (the Level A + AA subset),
adding its own engine-specific fields (rule coverage, automatability class).
Attribution: « WCAG 2.2 — W3C ».

It ALSO reproduces, since the normative-text vendoring, the success criteria's
own wording and the terms WCAG defines — see the next section.

================================================================================
Bundled WCAG 2.2 normative text and glossary
================================================================================

The `text` and `terms` fields on each criterion in src/data/wcag.json, and its
`glossary` map (vendored at scripts/vendor/wcag-2.2-text.json), are derived from
the W3C source: the success-criterion fragments under guidelines/sc/ and the
term definitions under guidelines/terms/.

Source: https://github.com/w3c/wcag
Spec:   https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/

These are a DERIVATIVE work: the HTML fragments are converted to plain text
(markup stripped, notes and exception labels kept as labelled lines, the
fragment's own title/conformance-level/change chrome removed). No wording is
paraphrased, summarised, translated or reordered.

The W3C Document License permits this for software and its documentation:

  "To facilitate implementation of the technical specifications set forth in
   this document, anyone may prepare and distribute derivative works and
   portions of this document in software, in supporting materials accompanying
   software, and in documentation of software, PROVIDED that all such works
   include the notice below. HOWEVER, the publication of derivative works of
   this document for use as a technical specification is expressly prohibited."

ultra11y is software; it ships this text as an offline reference an auditor
looks a criterion up in, NOT as a republication of WCAG as a technical
specification. The required notice:

  Copyright © 2023 W3C®. This software or document includes material copied
  from or derived from "Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2",
  https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/.

